---
title: What's Next
description: Further resources for configuring and extending the Vonage Video React App.
---

Congratulations, you have successfully completed the tutorial! Copy the public VERA backend server URL from this Codespace and paste it into the learning path to generate your certificate of completion — you don't need to keep this Codespace open or the server running afterwards.

## What You Accomplished

- Understood how all frontend configuration flows through `vcrBuild.env.sh`
- Enabled and disabled feature flags for media controls, in-call tools, and room behaviour
- Configured display defaults including resolution, layout mode, bitrate, and frame rates
- Applied your changes by restarting the dev server and verified them in the browser

## Resources

- [Vonage Developer Portal](https://developer.vonage.com) — Documentation, guides, and API references for all Vonage products.
- [Vonage Video API Documentation](https://developer.vonage.com/en/video/overview) — In-depth guides for the Video API.
- [vonage-video-react-app on GitHub](https://github.com/Vonage/vonage-video-react-app) — Source code, full README with all configuration options, and contribution guidelines.
